            <div id="pnlJobDescription">
	
                <h3 class="postingHeader">Job Description and Duties</h3>
                <p class="postingContent">
                    <p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;;"><span style="font-family: Arial;"><strong>Why Join DHCS?<br /><br /></strong> </span></span>The Department of Health Care Services (DHCS) is the backbone of California’s health care safety net. Our success is made possible by the hard work of more than 4,800 DHCS team members and through collaboration with the federal government and other state agencies, counties, and partners for the care of low-income families, children, pregnant women, older adults, and persons with disabilities. This is an exciting opportunity to join our diverse team in the following role. If you are interested in joining our team, apply today!</span></p><p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span><br /><strong> </strong></span></span><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><strong>About this Role:</strong><br /><br /> </span><span style="font-size: 12pt;">The Nurse Consultant (NC) I is  responsible for monitoring and evaluation of the licensing of Psychiatric Residential Treatment Facilities (PRTFs), Psychiatric Health Facilities (PHFs) and Mental Health Rehabilitation Centers (MHRCs). The NCI will travel and conduct in-depth licensing inspections of these facilities, conduct investigations of complaints and unusual incidents regarding client medical care, prepare comprehensive written narrative reports of investigations and inspections, including conclusions and recommendations, and prepares written statements of deficiencies when deemed  appropriate, advise and provide technical assistance to administrators regarding state mental health licensing facility requirements for uniform application of and compliance with state and federal laws, rules, and regulations pertaining to client care, including nursing, physician, pharmacy, social, and related service and respond to legal actions as an expert witness, Primary responsibility is for uniform application of and compliance with state and federal laws, rules and regulations pertaining to the clinical care of clients/patients received in DHCS licensed mental health facilities, which will include evaluation and consultation on the subjects of regulatory requirements, facility policy and procedure, nursing care services, physician services, pharmacy services, dietetic services and social and other related services. Responsibilities and duties include varied and complex tasks related to inspections, investigations, surveys, and evaluations of mental health facilities overseen by Mental Health Licensing Branch.<br /><br />Travel, including overnight, by airplane, train, automobile, and other transportation, up to 30% of the time, is required.<br /><br /></span></p><p style="font-size: 13.5pt; text-align: left; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span><span>Have questions and/or need assistance? Contact <a href="mailto:Recruit@dhcs.ca.gov" style="text-decoration: none;"><span style="color: #0563c1; text-decoration: underline;">Recruit@dhcs.ca.gov</span></a></span><span>, we are here to help walk you through the state hiring process! <br /><br />This position is subject to the Department’s Conflict of Interest Code and filing a Statement of Economic Interests (Form 700) when assuming this position, annually by April 1, and when leaving this position.<br /><br /></span></span></span></p><p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;">This position has been advertised as &quot;Until Filled&quot;. <br /><br /></span></span></p><p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt;"></span></p><p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"> </span></span></p><p style="text-align: left; margin: 0pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial;">&nbsp;</span></span></p><p>You will find additional information about the job in the <strong><a href='https://www.CalCareers.ca.gov/CalHrPublic/FileDownload.aspx?aid=26279327&name=808-959-8197-XXXNCIDSPosting.pdf' target='_blank'>Duty Statement</a></strong>.</p>
                </p>
            
